WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Planetary digest v1.0 — planetary-digest (en) · elevenlabs:eleven_v4_turbo

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:09.572
<v Narrator>Welcome to the OpenIE Research Radio Planetary Digest, summarizing 29 open-access studies on verifiable, energy-accounted computing.

2
00:00:09.652 --> 00:00:24.302
<v Narrator>Across our 4-stage lookup-first cascade, fast constant-time hash tables, trigram search indexes, and exact integer solvers handle routine queries locally, waking large neural models only as a last resort.

3
00:00:24.382 --> 00:00:45.604
<v Narrator>On inline 5-volt board shunts with 0.09 to 0.11 percent idle drift, unpacking 0.1517 bits-per-weight matrices back to 32-bit floats wasted 81.86 times more board energy than 8-bit integers, whereas packed integer logic dropped to 187.49 microjoules gross and cut full cascade energy 26.58 times.

4
00:00:45.684 --> 00:01:00.190
<v Narrator>Every study ships with cryptographic hashes, 6-fabric cross-architecture determinism, 24-kilobit Opus low-bandwidth feeds, extended audio description, and Creative Commons Zero plain-language summaries.
